<interrogationes unitas="imago">

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I load a PNG or JPEG file into pixels I can draw?
    <responsum symbolum="imago_caricare_ex_file imago_caricare_ex_memoria ImagoFructus Imago" via="tools/icones_instrumentum.c">Call
      imago_caricare_ex_file(via, piscina) (a NUL-terminated C path, not
      a chorda) or imago_caricare_ex_memoria(datum, mensura, piscina) and
      check fructus.successus before touching fructus.imago. The pixels
      are always 4 bytes per pixel, R, G, B, A, not premultiplied, rows
      top to bottom, whatever the file held (grey, palette and 16-bit
      images are converted to 8-bit RGBA). They live in your piscina;
      there is nothing to free.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I get the width and height of an image without decoding it?
    <responsum symbolum="imago_mensuras_ex_file imago_mensuras_ex_memoria" via="lib/imago.worklog.md">imago_mensuras_ex_file
      or imago_mensuras_ex_memoria read only the header (stbi_info) and
      allocate no pixels. They return FALSUM and set both outputs to 0
      when the file is missing or the format unknown. Both output
      pointers are written unconditionally, so they must not be
      NIHIL.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I find out why an image failed to load?
    <responsum symbolum="ImagoFructus imago_caricare_ex_file">Read
      fructus.error, a chorda (not NUL-terminated) copied into the
      piscina you passed: stb_image's short English failure reason, or
      "Argumenta invalida" for a NIHIL path, NIHIL data or zero length.
      With a NIHIL piscina the error is an empty chorda, since there is
      nowhere to copy the text. On success error is empty.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can I include imago.h just to use the Imago type without pulling in the decoder?
    <responsum symbolum="Imago" via="include/imago_typus.h">Include
      imago_typus.h instead: it declares Imago alone. imago.h brings
      lib/imago.c and vendor/stb_image.h into the link closure of every
      program that includes it, which once dragged the decoder into
      every app through vitrea. Writers (imago_png) and comparers
      (imago_collatio) use the type header only.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can a very large image make loading fail gracefully instead of exiting?
    <responsum symbolum="imago_caricare_ex_file piscina_allocare">Only
      if stb_image itself refuses it. The decoded buffer is malloc'd by
      stb_image and then copied into your piscina with piscina_allocare,
      which exits the process when it cannot get memory, so the
      "Non possum allocare memoriam" branch never returns in practice.
      Peak memory is about twice the RGBA size during the copy. Check
      the size first with imago_mensuras_ex_file.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I save pixels as a PNG file?
    <responsum symbolum="imago_png_scribere imago_png_codificare imago_ex_tabula">Not
      with this library, which only decodes. imago_png_scribere and
      imago_png_codificare write an Imago; imago_ex_tabula
      (delineare_mandata.h) views a TabulaPixelorum as an Imago without
      copying.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

</interrogationes>
